 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the public authorities law, in relation to the membership of\nthe board of directors of the New York city water board",
    "basePrintNo": "S4725",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S4725-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §1045-f, Pub Auth L",
    "lawSection": "Public Authorities Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S4725\n\nSPONSOR: SANDERS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the public authorities law, in relation to the member-\nship of the board of directors of the New York city water board\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo amend the New York City Water Board to include the five NYC Borough\nPresidents.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1.Subdivision 2 of section 1045-f of the public authorities law,\nas added by chapter 513 of the laws of 1984, is amended to include the\nborough president of each borough of the city of New York, the mayor or\na public member appointed by the mayor and a public member appointed by\nthe governor who has experience in the science of water resource devel-\nopment.\n\nSection 2 is the effective date.\n\n \nEXISTING LAW:\n\nThere is currently no civil cause of action for workplace abuse.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nCurrently, the Water Board consists of seven members appointed by the\nMayor. In addition, the Mayor appoints the Chairman from the members he\nselects for the Board. A majority of the members constitutes a quorum\nfor the transaction of any business, including raising the water rate.\n\nThis legislation changes the composition of the Water Board to include\nthe five Borough Presidents of New York city as part of the seven member\nBoard. It will give fair representation on establishing fee rates on any\nfuture water hikes by including a voice from each Borough for input in\ndiscussions and having a vote at the table. City residents and busi-\nnesses will feel their individual concerns can be represented and taken\ninto account during any negotiations that could result in a water rate\nhike.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2021-22 REFERRED TO SENATE CORPORATIONS, AUTHORITIES AND COMMISSIONS\n\n2021-22 referred to assembly corporations, authorities and commissions\n\n2019-20 REFERRED TO SENATE CORPORATIONS, AUTHORITIES AND COMMISSIONS\n\n2019-20 referred to assembly corporations, authorities and commissions\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n \nLOCAL FISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
